WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.168
Zann froze as Zing snorted and spurted out a puff of smoke.

2
00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:07.244
But the little dragon was only turning over in his sleep.

3
00:00:07.245 --> 00:00:10.717
Soon he was snoring in harmony with Darb once again.

4
00:00:10.718 --> 00:00:14.328
Rubbing his fingers, Zann touched the note he'd just written.

5
00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:18.614
It disappeared, though he could still feel the paper under his fingers.

6
00:00:18.615 --> 00:00:21.442
He hoped he'd performed the Vanishing spell correctly.

7
00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:26.012
If he had, the note would reappear in exactly three hours.

8
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:29.176
He glanced at Darb's sleeping form, feeling guilty.

9
00:00:29.177 --> 00:00:34.320
The note explained where Zann was going and why—just in case he never made it back.

10
00:00:34.321 --> 00:00:38.610
Zann tiptoed out of the room. Then he zapped himself to the palace.

11
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:45.408
When he saw the hulking guard standing outside the main entrance, he realized he hadn't thought his plan through very well.

12
00:00:45.409 --> 00:00:49.719
Powerful Shield spells stopped people from zapping into the palace uninvited.

13
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.286
How was he going to get inside?

14
00:00:52.287 --> 00:00:55.384
Just then the guard looked up and spotted him.

15
00:00:55.385 --> 00:01:00.429
"Zann!" he exclaimed. "Is that really you? What an honor!"

16
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.480
"Oh," Zann said in surprise. "Um, thanks."

17
00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:09.644
"Are the king and queen expecting you, or do you need me to wake them?" the guard asked.

18
00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:12.211
"Shall I show you to the throne room?"

19
00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:18.165
Zann was amazed. At last his new celebrity status was coming in handy!

20
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:23.219
"Thanks, but I remember the way," he told the guard, trying to sound casual.

21
00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.724
"And you don't need to wake anybody."

22
00:01:25.725 --> 00:01:33.873
Zann hurried inside. Only a few flickering candles lit the palace halls, but Zann had no trouble finding his way to the main courtyard.

23
00:01:33.874 --> 00:01:39.512
He shuddered as he glanced at the spot where Morb's monstrous magic-sucking machine had stood.

24
00:01:39.513 --> 00:01:42.980
Then he headed toward a balcony jutting from the second floor.

25
00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:46.643
He levitated to it and stepped into the hallway beyond.

26
00:01:46.644 --> 00:01:50.372
Spotting the door he wanted, he opened it and stepped inside.

27
00:01:50.373 --> 00:01:53.216
"Oops," he whispered as he looked around.

28
00:01:53.217 --> 00:01:55.698
He was in a bedroom he'd never seen before.

29
00:01:55.699 --> 00:02:02.881
A stout older man was snoring. Luckily the man didn't wake up as Zann quickly backed out of the room.

30
00:02:02.882 --> 00:02:05.448
Zann glanced up and down the hall.

31
00:02:05.449 --> 00:02:10.136
Okay, if that wasn't the right door, then surely it was the next one down . . .

32
00:02:10.137 --> 00:02:15.901
But the second door he opened revealed only a linen closet. And the third opened onto a deserted dining room.

33
00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:20.952
Zann stood in the hallway, trying to figure out why he couldn't find the room he wanted.

34
00:02:20.953 --> 00:02:29.103
"This is stupid," he muttered. Rubbing his hands together, he took a moment to focus his mind. "Zap," he whispered.

35
00:02:29.104 --> 00:02:34.301
He landed in a storage room. He smiled, sure he'd finally found the right room.

36
00:02:34.302 --> 00:02:40.587
But Zann's smile faded as he realized the room's window overlooked the aviary in the palace menagerie.

37
00:02:40.588 --> 00:02:46.083
This wasn't the right storage room. It wasn't even in the same part of the palace.

38
00:02:46.084 --> 00:02:52.506
"Drat," he muttered. Zann carefully pictured the right storage room in his mind. "Zap!"

39
00:02:52.507 --> 00:02:55.834
This time he landed in the palace library.

40
00:02:55.835 --> 00:02:59.056
He zapped again and ended up in the banquet hall.

41
00:02:59.057 --> 00:03:02.561
"Zann?" a familiar voice said. "What are you doing here?"

42
00:03:02.562 --> 00:03:08.783
Zann spun around. Yog sat at the table in his pajamas, feasting on wiggle root pie.

43
00:03:08.784 --> 00:03:16.324
"Yog!" Zann exclaimed. "Um, hi. I just came to, uh . . ." He thought fast.

44
00:03:16.325 --> 00:03:18.892
"To get something Boz left here earlier.

45
00:03:18.893 --> 00:03:23.799
But Boz said it was near the wormhole, and I can't seem to find the right room."

46
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.356
Yog looked surprised. "Didn't Boz warn you that you wouldn't be able to get to it?

47
00:03:28.357 --> 00:03:32.318
The Red Council didn't like having a wormhole inside the palace.

48
00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:36.320
Anyone or anything could wander through from another world."

49
00:03:36.321 --> 00:03:41.824
Zann was confused. "Then why didn't they do something about it sooner?" he asked.

50
00:03:41.825 --> 00:03:44.754
"You know how wormholes work," said Yog.

51
00:03:44.755 --> 00:03:47.284
"They can appear or disappear at random.

52
00:03:47.285 --> 00:03:50.888
We didn't know that one was in the palace until Morb used it."

53
00:03:50.889 --> 00:03:55.848
"Are the king and queen afraid that Morb might try to come back?" Zann asked.

54
00:03:55.849 --> 00:04:02.947
"I doubt it," Yog said. "Once you destroyed Morb's magic-sucking machine, he went back to being a Void, remember?

55
00:04:02.948 --> 00:04:10.518
It takes powerful magic to navigate the vortex connecting the wormholes. Morb will probably be lost forever."

56
00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:15.821
Zann thought anxiously of his parents. Were they still lost in the vortex, just like Morb?

57
00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:19.137
Thinking of them brought Zann's mind back to his quest.

58
00:04:19.138 --> 00:04:25.897
"So what happened?" he asked. "Did the Red Council close up the wormhole, or blow it up or something?"

59
00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:31.736
Yog shook his head. "Even the strongest magic can't destroy a wormhole," he explained.

60
00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:39.536
"All the Magic Masters joined together to block it off with a special Repel spell paired with an extra-strong Containment spell."

61
00:04:39.537 --> 00:04:45.046
"So that's what Boz and Teplo were doing here at the palace all day," Zann said.

62
00:04:45.047 --> 00:04:48.730
"Right," Yog said, taking another bite of his pie.

63
00:04:48.731 --> 00:04:53.156
"Okay. I should get home," Zann said. "See you later."

64
00:04:53.157 --> 00:05:00.623
He zapped himself out of the palace and stood in the moonlit courtyard outside, feeling frustrated. Now what?

65
00:05:00.624 --> 00:05:04.996
With the palace wormhole blocked, there was only one other option.

66
00:05:04.997 --> 00:05:09.280
Before he had time to get nervous, Zann muttered, "Zap!"

67
00:05:09.281 --> 00:05:11.928
Wormwood was a scary place at night.

68
00:05:11.929 --> 00:05:18.615
Moonlight shone through the branches of the gnarled old tree, casting spooky shadows over the ramshackle huts.

69
00:05:18.616 --> 00:05:23.857
Strange smells and stranger sounds drifted on the night breeze.

70
00:05:23.858 --> 00:05:30.120
Doing his best to ignore the creepy atmosphere, Zann stepped toward the tree's massive trunk.

71
00:05:30.121 --> 00:05:38.973
The wormhole opened, and Zann stared into its spinning, pulsating depths, feeling terrified and dizzy. Could he do this?

72
00:05:38.974 --> 00:05:42.529
Zann thought of his parents and knew he had to try.

73
00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.211
Holding his breath, he stuck one leg into the wormhole.

74
00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:54.530
A second later he felt the vortex's powerful energy pulling him in.

